From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:59:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayerAudio: trim audio overlap at Blu-ray seamless
 joins

Blu-ray packets are on title time, so the authored audio overlap of a
seamless join reaches the audio player as a pts step back. It builds up
across joins until the 50 ms sync correction fires and holds a video
frame, in passthrough and in PCM alike. Decoded audio can drop single
samples, while passthrough frames cannot be cut.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDStreamInfo.cpp    |  2 +
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDStreamInfo.h      |  1 +
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp      |  2 +
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerAudio.cpp | 61 +++++++++++++++++++++
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerAudio.h   |  2 +
 5 files changed, 68 insertions(+)

